  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Preheat oven to 200°C/180°C fan-forced.\n• Slice mini flour tortillas into quarters.\n• Thinly slice carrot into half-moons.\n• Finely chop garlic.\n• Drain sweetcorn.\n• Drain and rinse red kidney beans.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-66a9cd4c1960f8a32f0bf972-e42eb41f.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Spread mini flour tortilla chips over the lined oven tray (don’t worry if they overlap).\n• Drizzle with olive oil and season with salt. Sprinkle with Cheddar cheese. Bake until lightly golden and crisp, 8-10 minutes.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-66a9cd4c1960f8a32f0bf972-94c0fca6.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Meanwhile, in a large saucepan, heat a drizzle of olive oil over medium-high heat. Cook carrot and corn, stirring, until tender, 4-5 minutes.\n• SPICY! The spice blend is hot, use less if you're sensitive to heat. Add garlic, Mexican Fiesta spice blend and red kidney beans and cook until fragrant, 1-2 minutes.\n• Stir in diced tomatoes with garlic & onion, vegetable stock powder, the water and brown sugar until combined. Bring to a boil, then reduce heat to medium. Simmer, until slightly reduced, 3-4 minutes.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-66a9cd4c1960f8a32f0bf972-3872fc0d.jpeg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Remove saucepan from heat. Stir in baby spinach leaves and the butter, until wilted. Season to taste.\n• Divide Mexican tomato and bean soup between bowls.\n• Tear over coriander. Dollop over light sour cream. Serve with cheesy tortilla chips. Enjoy!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/recipe/step-66a9cd4c1960f8a32f0bf972-e3a327b3.jpeg"
    }
  ]
}
